    "body": "### Bug description\n\nCan't make calls between two Android smart phones. One has SIM card (PH1) and another (PH2) doesn't. \n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCall frfom PH1 (with SIM) to PH2 (without SIM), scenario 1::\n- PH1: start new call\n- phone PH1 makes sonar sound until it gets canceled by user \n- PH2 gets message \"Missed call from PH1\"\n\nCall frfom PH1 to PH2, scenario 2::\n- PH1: start new call\n- PH1 makes sonar sound, then start ringing. PH2 gets incoming call, user answers,\n- PH1 goes into \"Ringing\" state, PH2 goes into \"Answering\" state. There is no call acceptance.\n- After a while both PH1 and PH2 abandons call practically at the same time.\n- PH2 gets message in its info bar: \"Incoming Signal call (time stamp)\". If you click on it, it opens empty page without any control elements or a way to stop it. Only \"back\" will close it temporary...\n- There is no any way to remove that message from info bar. Even killing Signal doesn't help. The only solution at that point is to reboot the phone...\n\nCall from PH2 to PH1 doesn't work at all :\n- In PH2 make a call to PH1\n- Standard phone dialer appears. When user clicks on its \"call\" button, there is message \"Not registered on network\"\n\n**Actual result:** \nMaking call from PH1 to PH2 in both scenarios doesn't work. In second scenario PH2 has to reboot to get rid of notification message \"\"Incoming Signal call\". Call from PH2 to PH1 not possible at all too..\n\n**Expected result:**\nCall is accepted and proceed in both directions.\n### Device info\n\nPH1: **Device:\\* _Samsung Note II\n*_Android version:** 4.4.2\n**Signal version:** 3.15.2\nPH2: **Device:\\* _Samsung InFuse\n*_Android version:** 2.3.6\n**Signal version:** 3.15.2\n",
